// Let me understand the inductive proof structure
// 
// For client_send, the transition:
// 1. Removes client j from Idle to Waiting with rid=request.rid
// 2. Sets slot j to true
// 3. Deposits request j => request
// 
// The invariants that need to be preserved:
// 1. not_waiting_inv: forall |i: nat| valid_idx(i) && clients.index(i).is_Idle() ==> !slots.index(i)
// 2. waiting_inv: forall |i: nat| client_waiting(i) ==> request_stored(i) || response_stored(i) || combiner_has(i)
// 
// For client_send:
// - Before: client j is Idle, slot j may be false or true (cur_slot), request NOT stored
// - After: client j is Waiting, slot j is true, request j IS stored
// 
// For not_waiting_inv in post state:
// - For i != j: If post.clients.index(i).is_Idle(), then we need !post.slots.index(i)
//   Since client i wasn't changed, pre.clients.index(i) == post.clients.index(i)
//   and pre.slots.index(i) == post.slots.index(i), so this holds by pre.not_waiting_inv
// - For i == j: post.clients.index(j) is Waiting, not Idle, so the implication is vacuously true
// 
// For waiting_inv in post state:
// - For i != j: If post.client_waiting(i), then pre.client_waiting(i) (unchanged)
//   So by pre.waiting_inv, we have pre.request_stored(i) || pre.response_stored(i) || pre.combiner_has(i)
//   We need to show this holds in post too (which it does, since those predicates don't change for i != j)
// - For i == j: post.client_waiting(j) is true (client is now Waiting)
//   We need to show: post.request_stored(j) || post.response_stored(j) || post.combiner_has(j)
//   We have post.request_stored(j) because we deposited the request!
// 
// The key is to prove that the invariants are preserved for ALL i, not just the changed ones.

